{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "9f2c1a44-7d3e-4c1b-9a10-idiotpedals00",
    "name": "Idiot Pedals",
    "description": "Idiot Pedals API — every endpoint, matching the code (folders: Health, Auth, Users, Products, Orders, Payments, Webhooks).\n\nWARNING — REAL SIDE EFFECTS\n- Register, a COD order (paymentMethod \"cod\") and Verify Payment all send a REAL email to ADMIN_ORDER_EMAIL unless the server runs with EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=false. Start the API with that flag set while you test: `EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=false npm run dev`.\n- Use Razorpay TEST keys only (rzp_test_...). Never point this collection at live keys.\n\nSETUP\n- Set {{baseUrl}} in your Postman environment (e.g. http://localhost:5000) and select the environment before running anything.\n- Login saves {{accessToken}} automatically. Endpoints that need an admin (create/update/delete product) require the token of an admin account.\n- Register and Login bodies contain placeholders (PASTE_...). Replace them with a real test account you control; they are intentionally not variables so no credential is stored in this file.\n- The Razorpay verify body needs the values Razorpay Checkout hands back to the browser. {{razorpayOrderId}} is saved by Create payment; {{razorpayPaymentId}} and {{razorpaySignature}} come from the checkout response.\n- The Razorpay webhook request signs its own raw body in a pre-request script using {{razorpayWebhookSecret}} from the environment (server-to-server only — the frontend never calls it).\n\nGoogle OAuth requests return 302. Turn OFF \"Automatically follow redirects\" in Postman settings, otherwise 302 becomes the final page status.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:5000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "orderId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "productId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "razorpayOrderId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "razorpayPaymentId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "razorpaySignature", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
